{
  "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
  "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The participants in the ratification debates disagreed about whether the new constitution would, or should, subject states to suit in the new courts of the soon-to-be superior sovereign, but they were unanimous in their understanding that states could not be sued in the courts of other states."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What is new from -- MR. WAXMAN: Are -- you say the original case. Do you mean Nevada versus Hall? JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Franchise Tax Board of California",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the only case in state or federal court in the 200 years prior that had ever recognized the ability of one state to compel another state to answer. It cited zero cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We've already recognized them. This turned -- this turned from a multimillion-dollar case into, what, a $100,000 case now?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professors Baude and Sachs",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Baude and Sachs. Professors Baude and Sachs acknowledge that there was a universal rule in the law of nations. Their argument is it wasn't constitutionalized; it just stayed some sort of common law rule. It wasn't abrogated, but it wasn't constitutionalized."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: How -- how should we think about the fact that 47 or 45 or whatever it is states have joined in this amicus brief, indicating that they think that their sovereign immunity power is a good deal more important than the power that you've referenced to protect their own citizens in their own courts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Have there been attempts by the states to -- to enter into agreements of this sort?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Should we regard the submissions of the Solicitor General here as reflecting the views of the United States or simply the Solicitor General?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could the Nevada court have adjudicated the factual premises? Could he have brought some sort of suit in Nevada to adjudicate whether he was a resident of California or not or to find that he had no tax liability?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chemerinsky",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has plenary power over Indian tribes. This has been understood since the founding to exclude state interference with Indian affairs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chemerinsky",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
      "evidence_id": "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CHEMERINSKY: Well, I'd go back to this Court's decision in the Hilton versus South Carolina case, and this Court there said adherence to precedent promotes stability, predictability, and respect for judicial authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1299",
